# B-line IL, B6 §4: one axis step

At axis `k` the registers hold (`vK`): `σ 0..3 = p, α, h, d`, `σ 4 = #ones`, `σ 5 = T`,
`σ 6 = pre_k`, `σ 8 = k`, `σ 13 = bits_{≥k}`, `σ 14 = bits_{<k}` (reversed), `σ 15 = s_{<k}`
(reversed); `dS = s_{≥k}`.

`axP1`: `σ 9 := b_k`, `σ 10 := s_k` (both also saved on `σ 14`, `σ 15`), `σ 11 := t_k = 2^h (1 +
b_k)`, `σ 7 := post_k = T / (pre_k t_k)`; then `descAx6` is pushed on `dA` by `dup`, `eX` is
called, the descriptor dropped; `axP2`: pop `σ 9, 10, 7`, `σ 6 := pre_k t_k`, pop `σ 11`,
`σ 8 := k + 1`.
-/

